      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U3", "C13"],
      "pins": ["U3.28", "C13.1", "C13.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U3-VCC)", "GND", "VCC"],
      "observed": "The SSD1306 pin 28 is named VCC and is typed as power_in, but in the netlist it is only connected to C13 (2.2 uF) to GND on the local net Net-(U3-VCC). It is not connected to the board VCC rail.",
      "expected": "A power_in supply pin such as the SSD1306 VCC pin should be connected to a valid supply rail (here VCC), with C13 acting as its bypass/filter capacitor. The specification also describes this pin as a supply pin: 'C7 (2.2 µF) — U4 VCC (digital-logic supply pin) to GND'.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"22\") (name \"Net-(U3-VCC)\") ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"28\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ... (node (ref \"C13\") (pin \"1\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"C13\") (pin \"2\") ...))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "`C7` (2.2 µF) — U4 `VCC` (digital-logic supply pin) to GND"}
      ],
      "impact": "The OLED driver's VCC pin would have no DC path to the power rail, leaving the display supply floating. This would likely prevent the OLED from initializing or operating correctly.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The connectivity otherwise matches the specification after reference renumbering, but the SSD1306 VCC power pin is left on a bypass-capacitor-only local net instead of being connected to the VCC rail, which is a likely board-behavior anomaly."
}

